  "toyota_summary": "Germany's largest labor union is threatening strikes after a major automaker announced it will terminate multiple wage agreements starting January 1, 2027. The company cited competitive pressure and rising costs. Union leaders have already begun mobilizing, signaling they will not accept the move without a fight.\n\nFor the industry, this signals a broader collision between legacy automakers' need to cut costs amid the transition to electric vehicles and European labor's determination to protect wages. Germany accounts for roughly a quarter of European auto production, and labor unrest there can ripple across supply chains. A prolonged dispute could disrupt manufacturing at a moment when the sector can least afford it.\n\nWatch whether other German manufacturers follow suit or try to negotiate differently, which will signal how far companies are willing to push labor in 2025.",
